infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Long-lived JWT vs short access + rotating refresh
  desc The same stateless token — valid for 90 days, or killable within 15 minutes
  compares
    - label Long-lived JWT (no refresh)
      children
        - label Fully stateless, scales freely
          desc No session store on the hot path; every read needs zero DB lookups
        - label A signed token can't be un-issued
          desc No logout, no denylist — valid until exp no matter what you delete
        - label Revoked access lingers ~90 days
          desc signOptions expiresIn '90d' — an ex-employee's token works for weeks
    - label Short access + rotating refresh
      children
        - label Stateless reads, 15-minute access TTL
          desc signOptions expiresIn '15m' bounds the compromise window to minutes
        - label Refresh token is revocable
          desc Stored server-side (row/Redis), rotated each use, deletable on demand
        - label Kill a session within ~15 minutes
          desc Delete the refresh token; next refresh fails, access dies on TTL
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
